# Keep both sides when two people append at once, instead of raising a conflict.
# Without this, two ideas added at the same time collide at the end of the file and
# one person's entry gets lost during the rebase — the worst possible failure here.
IDEAS.md merge=union
CONTEXT.md merge=union
JOURNAL.md merge=union
TASKS.md merge=union

# Journey files are deliberately NOT listed here. They're edited in place rather
# than appended to, so union-merging a flowchart would duplicate nodes and produce
# a diagram that renders as nonsense — two people rewriting the same flow should
# get a real conflict and talk to each other.
#
# The union rules above are per-file, so journeys already fall through to git's
# normal text merge, which is exactly what's wanted. An earlier version wrote
# `journeys/*.md -merge=union` intending "don't union-merge these". That actually
# UNSETS the merge attribute, which makes git treat the file as binary and refuse
# to merge it at all — "Cannot merge binary files", no conflict markers, nothing a
# person or Claude can resolve. Don't reintroduce it.

